  "description": "Reid Pulse SO | Urban Commuter eBike\nUrban comfort. Effortless everyday riding.\nRedefine your daily commute with the Reid Bikes Pulse SO eBike, a sleek, modern urban hybrid eBike designed to make every ride effortless, comfortable, and stylish. Built around a lightweight alloy frame with clean internal cable routing and a fully integrated downtube battery, the Pulse combines contemporary design with everyday practicality.\nThe Reid Bikes Pulse SO eBike is powered by a reliable Ananda M131 250W rear hub motor, delivering smooth, natural-feeling assistance which is paired with a 7 speed Shimano drive chain to make climbing hills easier and navigating busy city streets a breeze. The 36V 11.6Ah (417Wh) battery provides plenty of range for daily commuting, errands, and weekend rides, while the Bluetooth-enabled Ananda D19 display connects seamlessly to your smartphone, allowing you to track ride data and navigate with confidence.\nDesigned to excel in the urban environment, the Reid Bikes Pulse SO pairs dependable performance with all-day comfort. Shimano hydraulic disc brakes deliver powerful, consistent braking in all conditions, while wide, high-volume tyres help smooth out uneven terrain for a more comfortable ride. An adjustable alloy stem, ergonomic lock-on grips, and a plush comfort saddle create an upright riding position that enhances comfort, confidence, and visibility. Additional accessories include full mudguards to help keep you clean and dry, a practical rear rack that's perfect for carrying shopping or work essentials, and a sturdy kickstand for convenient parking during quick stops or easy storage. Whether you're heading to work or popping to the shops, the Reid Pulse eBike transforms everyday journeys into something you'll look forward to.\nWho is the Reid Bikes Pulse SO eBike for?\nThe Pulse is ideal for:\n\nHow far can the Pulse travel on a full charge?\nThe Pulse can deliver up to approximately 56km of range on a full charge under ideal conditions. Actual range will vary depending on rider weight, luggage, terrain, wind, tyre pressure, temperature and the level of electric assistance used.\nPlease make sure to familiarise yourself with eBike and eScooter safety information before charging or using your new Reid. You can view and download user manuals and safety instructions here.",
